  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive). Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{宥|なだ}める.\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed when dealing with someone in an emotional state — crying, angry, or panicking. The subject is always trying to restore calm through words, gestures, or comfort.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{子供|こども}→子供：00554_kodomo⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{宥|なだ}める: to soothe a child\n- ⟦{怒|いか}り→怒り：01780_ikari⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{宥|なだ}める: to calm someone's anger\n- ⟦{泣|な}いている→泣く：00655_naku⟧⟦{人|ひと}→人：00476_hito⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{宥|なだ}める: to comfort someone who is crying\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n⟦{落|お}ち{着|つ}かせる→落ち着く：04670_ochitsuku⟧ means \"to make someone calm down\" and is more neutral. {宥|なだ}める implies a gentler, more soothing approach, often with words of comfort. ⟦{慰|なぐさ}める→慰める：02133_nagusameru⟧ (to console) focuses more on emotional comfort after loss or sadness, whereas {宥|なだ}める focuses on calming active distress.",
